I want to know we're cared about and we  all want to be cared about equally and  on that subject my talk at the table is  the u.s. women's soccer team one of the  most successful female sports teams in  American history but the players have  been arguing that they are not being  treated the same as the men's team but a  federal judge threw out the equal pay  claim in their lawsuit on Friday though  he will allow them to go forward and  fight other issues like travel and  medical support a trial is now set for  June and the team's co-captain Megan  Rapinoe is going to join us now from  Greenwich Connecticut Megan good morning  good morning how are you doing this is  how we're doing all right we appreciate  you continuing to come on and talk about  this case so publicly and being so  transparent about it I think the first  question has to be this has been a four  year fight you were asking for 67  million in back pay at a minimum and the  judge said nope through the whole thing  out what's your reaction  I mean shocked to be honest very shocked  and and of course disappointed in this I  didn't I didn't feel like the the ruling  really captured the heart of what we're  after if we were under the men's  contract which for the record we asked  to be an amend contract it was  repeatedly refused to us not only in the  structure but in the total compensation  if we were under that contract we would  you know earn at least three times  higher then we have the argument that  we've earned more over the course of the  time we're talking about then the men's  team really misses the hook merely says  the whole point we've won two World Cups  and we've won basically a game that we  played darn near so to have that  compared in that way and sort of missing  the fact that we've outperformed the  men's team just to say that we earned a  little bit more money I feel like really  misses the heart of the gender gender  discrimination suit that we've brought  against the Federation yeah well Megan  you touch on a really important point  here that is central to the judges  argument in in dismissing the pay  portion of this and neither one of us  are lawyers but I think as a matter of  public argument we can understand this  the judge is saying that the women could  have negotiated a different contract but  chose not to  and the man negotiated the one that they  did  you can't now go back and say hey we  wish we had done it differently that's  his position what's your response to  that as I'm sure many women who have  been in our position I can sympathize  with we did ask for the same for the  same contract and we asked for the same  amount of money and that was repeatedly  and then no one certain terms told to us  that that was not going to be possible  so for the for the ruling to sort of  imply that you know we were peachy King  with the original deal that we got and  now that we're understanding that we  could have had more money and so we're  going back on it is very frustrating for  us at the time we felt like we  negotiated the best deal that we were  offered but at the time it was very  clear as well that the money that we  were going to be paid or the money that  we could even negotiate with was going  to be far less than what was being  offered to the men yeah so the Women's  National Team has said they're going to  appeal you're gonna be part of that  appeal but the US Soccer Federation has  said they're looking forward to charting  a fair path forward those are their  words does that potentially mean there  could be a settlement here are you open  to that I think that we've been very  transparent about our openness to a  settlement ultimately what we want to  get to is something that's fair and  equal and if that comes in the form of a  settlement  we are definitely open to that I don't  think anybody is dying to go into  litigation or go to trial or go through  a lawsuit it's been a very arduous  process for us as players so we're  always open to that but with that we're  not going to settle we know what we're  worth we feel very strong in our case  even with this ruling maybe even even  stronger now so a settlement is always  on the table we'll will always have open  ears to that but it'll be nothing less  than well yeah I should clarify  something which is important here I said  that they wanted to chart a fair path  forward the exact word and the quote is  actually a positive path forward on that  front in these four years you've been  having this fight there have been  changes atop the leadership structure of  US soccer there's now a new president  Cindy cone she's a former member  of the Women's National Team I'm curious  is she reached out to you as a fellow  player to say hey let's work out a deal  I have not heard from her since the  ruling we haven't had a conversation  with her as players prior but I know the  kind of acts falls on on the head of the  president and I think that cindy has a  very big job ahead of her but I don't  think we can let the board off as well I  think that the Board of Directors has  you know huge decision decision-making  role within u.s. soccer and they always  have so I think they need to be a part  of this conversation as well and it  needs to come from bull Cindy who is  obviously the figurehead but from the  board as well and again always open that  conversation we are always willing to  listen but in the absence of something  that truly is fair and equal I'm not  sure a positive path is really what  we're after  yeah former Vice President Joe Biden  leading contender for the Democratic  presidential nomination has voiced his  support for your position saying if he's  vice if he's president or when he's  president he will push the equal pay  initiative is he part of your plan going  forward and and speaking of your  alliance with him I am curious you  appeared with him in a video interview  just a day before he appeared on Morning  Joe to address for the first time the  Torah Reed allegations since you've been  so closely lined with him and since he's  behind you in this fight for equality  what did you think of his reaction to  those allegations and how do they affect  the campaign I mean I think all  allegations of sexual assault need to be  taken very seriously  you know I welcome the media talking  about it and welcome a full  investigation I think that any woman who  comes forward deserves that in terms of  his support for the lawsuit we welcome  any and all support for both sides of  the aisle and we have had a lot of  support on both sides of the aisle  across the political spectrum about this  I think that this issue goes beyond  politics and goes beyond partisanship  and I think this is just an issue really  of human rights  of what is fair and equal under the law  all right Megan Rapinoe thank you again  for coming on to talk about this issue  we will have you on for the next chapter  appreciate it

